      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 6.18,
          "en": "So let's now output these expenses in a list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 6.18,
          "end": 8.67,
          "en": "And for that, I'll replace this Text widget here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.67,
          "end": 12.99,
          "en": "which acted as a placeholder, with an actual list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.99,
          "end": 17.85,
          "en": "But I'll not add this list here in this _ExpensesState,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.85,
          "end": 20.37,
          "en": "instead, I'll create a separate widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.37,
          "end": 22.89,
          "en": "to keep this widget or this state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.89,
          "end": 26.01,
          "en": "which belongs to the Expenses widget, lean,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.01,
          "end": 29.4,
          "en": "and to especially keep its build function lean and simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.4,
          "end": 32.16,
          "en": "Because that is considered a good practice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.16,
          "end": 34.53,
          "en": "keeping your build functions lean",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.53,
          "end": 37.62,
          "en": "and not putting too much logic into them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.62,
          "end": 40.83,
          "en": "That's typically what you want to strive for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.83,
          "end": 43.43,
          "en": "So therefore, here, I'll add a new file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.43,
          "end": 47.583,
          "en": "expenses_list.dart sounds like a fitting file name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.42,
          "end": 51.93,
          "en": "Because in there, I'll add a new class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.93,
          "end": 53.7,
          "en": "the ExpensesList class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.7,
          "end": 57.03,
          "en": "which now will be used for creating a widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.03,
          "end": 58.74,
          "en": "And therefore, this must extend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.74,
          "end": 61.98,
          "en": "one of Flutter's widget base classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.98,
          "end": 65.43,
          "en": "And here a StatelessWidget is all we need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.43,
          "end": 69.75,
          "en": "because we won't manage any internal data in that list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.75,
          "end": 73.11,
          "en": "Instead, we'll just output the list of expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 73.11,
          "end": 74.46000000000001,
          "en": "that is defined here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.46000000000001,
          "end": 77.1,
          "en": "We don't manage that list, we just output it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.1,
          "end": 79.86,
          "en": "And therefore, this will be a StatelessWidget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.86,
          "end": 82.77,
          "en": "And of course, it needs this build method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.77,
          "end": 84.48,
          "en": "And in this build method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.48,
          "end": 87.873,
          "en": "I then want to return my list in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.74,
          "end": 90.72,
          "en": "Now, before we create that list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.72,
          "end": 92.03999999999999,
          "en": "we, of course, must make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.03999999999999,
          "end": 94.74000000000001,
          "en": "that the ExpensesList widget class here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.74000000000001,
          "end": 98.10300000000001,
          "en": "accepts this list of expenses as input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.18,
          "end": 102.24000000000001,
          "en": "For that, we need to add the constructor function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.24000000000001,
          "end": 105.18299999999999,
          "en": "which here can be a const constructor function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.25999999999999,
          "end": 110.31,
          "en": "And of course, we want to forward that key as always.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.31,
          "end": 113.82,
          "en": "But then I'll accept more named parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.82,
          "end": 116.55,
          "en": "because I want to have some properties in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.55,
          "end": 119.58,
          "en": "To be precise, I'll start with one property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 119.58,
          "end": 123.54,
          "en": "we'll add another property later in this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.54,
          "end": 126.63,
          "en": "But this one property, which I'll add here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.63,
          "end": 129.45,
          "en": "is my list of expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 129.45,
          "end": 132.12,
          "en": "So here I'll use the built-in List type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.12,
          "end": 134.73,
          "en": "And it's a generic type, as you already know,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.73,
          "end": 137.67000000000002,
          "en": "and it is basically a list full of expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.67000000000002,
          "end": 140.49,
          "en": "Hence, I'll add my custom Expense class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 140.49,
          "end": 143.34,
          "en": "And by using this suggested option here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 143.34,
          "end": 146.79,
          "en": "my editor also automatically adds this import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.79,
          "end": 148.593,
          "en": "to the expense.dart file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 150.09,
          "end": 153.3,
          "en": "So here I'm using this Expense type here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 153.3,
          "end": 155.85,
          "en": "to combine it with the List type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 155.85,
          "end": 159.93,
          "en": "And then here this property can be named expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 159.93,
          "end": 164.88,
          "en": "And I now also have this required named expenses parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 164.88,
          "end": 169.47,
          "en": "which is used to assign a value to this expenses property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 169.47,
          "end": 172.14,
          "en": "And now we can use this expenses property here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 172.14,
          "end": 175.263,
          "en": "in the build method to output this list of expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 176.31,
          "end": 178.05,
          "en": "Now, thus far in the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 178.05,
          "end": 180.3,
          "en": "whenever we had multiple items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 180.3,
          "end": 182.1,
          "en": "that should be displayed above each other,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 182.1,
          "end": 183.663,
          "en": "we used the Column widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 184.68,
          "end": 186.6,
          "en": "And this is a great widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 186.6,
          "end": 189.48,
          "en": "for outputting widgets above each other.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 189.48,
          "end": 192.87,
          "en": "You can use it for a list content too, therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 192.87,
          "end": 197.73,
          "en": "But if you have lists of unclear length",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 197.73,
          "end": 200.85,
          "en": "that could potentially get quite long,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 200.85,
          "end": 203.94,
          "en": "as it is the case here, for this expenses list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 203.94,
          "end": 207.48,
          "en": "users could add 100 or 1,000 expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 207.48,
          "end": 209.4,
          "en": "when the app is up and running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 209.4,
          "end": 212.67000000000002,
          "en": "So when you have a list of unknown length",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 212.67000000000002,
          "end": 215.49,
          "en": "that will potentially get very long,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 215.49,
          "end": 217.53,
          "en": "Column is not ideal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 217.53,
          "end": 221.49,
          "en": "Because with Column, all the widgets that you add to it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 221.49,
          "end": 225.45,
          "en": "will be created behind the scenes by Flutter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 225.45,
          "end": 228.39,
          "en": "whenever this widget that outputs this Column",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 228.39,
          "end": 230.04,
          "en": "becomes active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 230.04,
          "end": 233.31,
          "en": "So that means if you have a list with 1,000 items,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 233.31,
          "end": 237.09,
          "en": "all these items will be created behind the scenes by Flutter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 237.09,
          "end": 239.73,
          "en": "at the point of time where this list widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 239.73,
          "end": 242.37,
          "en": "is displayed on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 242.37,
          "end": 244.23,
          "en": "The problem with that is, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 244.23,
          "end": 247.02,
          "en": "that only a small amount of those expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 247.02,
          "end": 249.87,
          "en": "is actually needed because only a small amount",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 249.87,
          "end": 252.69,
          "en": "of the expense list items that will display here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 252.69,
          "end": 254.94,
          "en": "will be visible on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 254.94,
          "end": 257.55,
          "en": "We will have a scrollable list, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 257.55,
          "end": 259.17,
          "en": "and most of those items, therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 259.17,
          "end": 261.42,
          "en": "won't be visible initially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 261.42,
          "end": 264.57,
          "en": "Hence, creating all these invisible items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 264.57,
          "end": 266.49,
          "en": "behind the scenes at the beginning",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 266.49,
          "end": 270.093,
          "en": "is really redundant and costs a lot of performance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 271.05,
          "end": 273.27,
          "en": "That's why you should not use Column",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 273.27,
          "end": 275.79,
          "en": "for lists where you don't know the length,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 275.79,
          "end": 278.553,
          "en": "but where you might have a lot of items at the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 279.51,
          "end": 281.85,
          "en": "Instead, Flutter gives you a different widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 281.85,
          "end": 284.15999999999997,
          "en": "that should be used for such situations,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 284.15999999999997,
          "end": 286.293,
          "en": "and that's the ListView widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 287.55,
          "end": 290.07,
          "en": "Now ListView can also be created like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 290.07,
          "end": 292.40999999999997,
          "en": "and you can pass children to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 292.40999999999997,
          "end": 295.35,
          "en": "If you do that, you get a scrollable list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 295.35,
          "end": 298.59000000000003,
          "en": "which still creates all items immediately",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 298.59000000000003,
          "end": 302.37,
          "en": "when this list is displayed on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 302.37,
          "end": 303.96,
          "en": "So the only thing we gain here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 303.96,
          "end": 306.96,
          "en": "is that this is automatically scrollable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 306.96,
          "end": 310.41,
          "en": "But it's still not ideal for this scenario here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 310.41,
          "end": 312.21,
          "en": "where we might have many items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 312.21,
          "end": 314.52,
          "en": "that won't be visible initially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 314.52,
          "end": 317.28,
          "en": "Instead, here we should not use ListView like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 317.28,
          "end": 320.61,
          "en": "but use a special constructor that's offered by it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 320.61,
          "end": 323.103,
          "en": "the builder constructor function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 324.27,
          "end": 326.94,
          "en": "This is a special constructor function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 326.94,
          "end": 329.01,
          "en": "for this ListView widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 329.01,
          "end": 330.54,
          "en": "which in the end tells Flutter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 330.54,
          "end": 333.48,
          "en": "that it should create a scrollable list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 333.48,
          "end": 337.59000000000003,
          "en": "ListViews are always scrollable lists by default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 337.59000000000003,
          "end": 340.98,
          "en": "But that it should build, create,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 340.98,
          "end": 344.4,
          "en": "those list items only when they are visible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 344.4,
          "end": 346.44,
          "en": "or about to become visible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 346.44,
          "end": 348.273,
          "en": "not if they're not visible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 349.23,
          "end": 352.74,
          "en": "For that, builder takes an itemBuilder parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 352.74,
          "end": 354.84000000000003,
          "en": "which is of type Function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 354.84000000000003,
          "end": 357.18,
          "en": "So which wants a function as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 357.18,
          "end": 359.67,
          "en": "And of course, you learned before in the course already",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 359.67,
          "end": 364.14,
          "en": "that you can pass functions as values for parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 364.14,
          "end": 366.15,
          "en": "So that's what we need to do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 366.15,
          "end": 368.22,
          "en": "And it wants a function that will get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 368.22,
          "end": 370.8,
          "en": "two input values itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 370.8,
          "end": 374.61,
          "en": "Those will be provided automatically by Flutter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 374.61,
          "end": 376.92,
          "en": "And it should then return a widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 376.92,
          "end": 380.49,
          "en": "So this function, which we pass as a value to itemBuilder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 380.49,
          "end": 382.05,
          "en": "should return a widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 382.05,
          "end": 384.513,
          "en": "the list item that should be created when needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 385.44,
          "end": 388.35,
          "en": "So for this here, I'll create an anonymous function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 388.35,
          "end": 390.63,
          "en": "You could also create a separate method here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 390.63,
          "end": 392.37,
          "en": "and then just point at it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
